  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reversing Environmental Degradation in Africa and Asia (REDAA) Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholder farmers make up 96% of the rural population of Rwanda and 70% of the total population. Land degradation, soil erosion, and deforestation impact ecosystems and livelihoods. Rwanda has well-written climate strategies and policies, but limited end-user understanding and community engagement constrain effective implementation. 

Through community-level research, Tearfund will assess the implementation and effectiveness of such policies in Huye and Gisagara districts, identified as most vulnerable to environmental degradation. Research findings will inform strategies and plans for evidence-based locally-led action in these local communities, for more integrated and sustainable community involvement and local solutions to reverse environmental degradation.</narrative>
  </description>
